+GCC is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY
+WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A
+PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the GNU General Public License for more details.
+
+You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License along with
+GCC; see the file COPYING3.  If not see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
+
+This header carries what the target mandates rather than what a caller
+remembers.  Everything in it is a value some package can forget to pass, which
+is the definition of a thing that belongs here instead of in a makefile.  The
+target definition it answers to is doc/target-definition.md.  */
+
+/* The red zone is honoured on this platform eventually, and not yet.  That
+   ordering is the whole content of this block, so it comes first.
+
+   The psABI reserves 128 bytes below %rsp and a conforming platform leaves
+   them alone.  The direction is to honour them at the delivery site, the way
+   a Linux kernel does, rather than to compile the world with a flag that
+   announces through every leaf's prologue that this is not quite the ABI it
+   claims to be.  DR-0006 records that direction and WP-43 is where it lands.
+   The flag below is scaffolding for the bootstrap and not the shipped answer.
+
+   What stands in the way is not Windows.  Spike 3 measured the host leaving
+   the reserved bytes alone under preemption, thread hijacking and its own
+   exception dispatch, and measured Cygwin's own signal delivery taking the
+   word at %rsp-8 on every single delivery.  So the two repairs are not
+   alternatives to choose between but steps in an order: until that delivery
+   path reserves the bytes before it builds a handler frame, an object
+   compiled with a red zone corrupts a stack at an unpredictable later date in
+   a package nobody was looking at.  Removing the flag first would not make
+   this platform more faithful to ELF; it would make every leaf a defect.
+
+   Hence the flag, and hence -mred-zone still turning it back on.  That escape
+   hatch is the point rather than a concession.  Spike 7 showed a delivery
+   that reserves the 128 bytes first keeps them whole across every delivery;
+   WP-43 has to price that against Cygwin's real sigdelayed and write the
+   record that retires the flag.  A target that refused the option outright
+   would force a toolchain rebuild before that measurement could be taken at
+   all.
+
+   DR-0006 made the choice between the two repairs and left WP-43 the price.
+   Nothing here makes either call; what this file does is keep both reachable
+   until the number exists.
+
+   Hand-written assembly is reached by none of this, which is why WP-16
+   delivers a ledger of it.
+   Added to i386/unix.h's set rather than replacing it, which is the whole of
+   the difficulty.  That header defines the default as MASK_80387, MASK_IEEE_FP
+   and MASK_FLOAT_RETURNS, and a target header that assigns instead of ORing
+   silently turns the x87 off.  Nothing complains at configure time; libgcc
+   fails much later building __mulxc3 with "x87 register return with x87
+   disabled", which reads like a libgcc bug and is not one.  */
+#undef  TARGET_SUBTARGET_DEFAULT
+#define TARGET_SUBTARGET_DEFAULT \
+	(MASK_80387 | MASK_IEEE_FP | MASK_FLOAT_RETURNS | MASK_NO_RED_ZONE)
+
+/* config.guess cannot read the vendor field off uname here: sysname is Linux
+   by design, so that the thousands of configure scripts branching on it keep
+   working.  It asks the compiler instead, the way it already asks which libc
+   it is looking at, and this is the answer it asks for.  Removing this define
+   makes a native build silently configure as x86_64-pc-linux-gnu.  */
+#undef  TARGET_OS_CPP_BUILTINS
+#define TARGET_OS_CPP_BUILTINS()		\
+  do						\
+    {						\
+      GNU_USER_TARGET_OS_CPP_BUILTINS ();	\
+      ANDROID_TARGET_OS_CPP_BUILTINS ();	\
+      builtin_define ("__ELFSYSVNT__");		\
+    }						\
+  while (0)
